{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>דוה</b> three times in the Masorah; the others: תזרם כמו דוה, כל היום דוה. Through ע\"ג (idolatry) she is impure like a menstruant, and because they served ע\"ג (idolatry), they caused: כל היום דוה (all the day [she is] sickly)." "<b>מקורה</b> two times in the Masorah; the other: והובשתי את מקורה. Because he emitted מקורה (her flow) dry — מקורה written: ערירים יהיו ולא תוליד." "<b>הערה</b> three times in the Masorah; the others: כי את שארו הערה, אשר הערה למות נפשו. Because he emitted שארו הערה (his fleshly emission) — הערה למות נפשו (an emission for the death of a soul) — he became liable to death with witnesses and warning." "<b>מקור דמיה</b> — read it דמי ה, שה, דמים טמאים באשה. In all of them, one is forbidden to commit adultery only with another man's wife, for HaShem is filled with anger against him that he forbids her to her husband."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "ע\"ג read as abbreviation for עבודה זרה (idolatry); the argument links idolatrous worship to the menstrual impurity of the congregation.", 1 "The argument turns on the dryness of the flow as punishment: the root יבש (dry) linked to barrenness.", 2 "The three occurrences of הערה are juxtaposed: the act of emission is read against the consequence of capital liability.", 3 "The qere/reshib reading splits מקור דמיה into דמי ה and שה; the latter is opaque and rendered as written."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:16.499678936Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}